    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d112">

                <pb facs="0224" n="108" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg108"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.811/127a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Minister Reinsch.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-05-18">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 18, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Chinese Minister for Foreign Affairs has telegraphed Legation here that there
                    is misunderstanding as to preliminary survey of the Hwai River, saying Wai Chiao
                    Pu never agreed to assume whole expense and that you informed him that Red Cross
                    expected to be reimbursed amount of its contribution. Inform Wai Chiao Pu that
                    the Red Cross is willing to contribute up to $50,000 gold without repayment if
                    no loan made and, with or without J. G. White Company, will advance the balance
                    up to $100,000 with understanding that such balance is to be refunded.</p>
                <p>Three eminent engineers, Sibert chairman, will leave for China about June
                    first.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
